{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystemSetup\/setLocalStoreDirectory(_:discardingExistingCache:)"},"defaultImplementationsSections":[{"title":"CloudFileSystemSetup Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystemSetup\/setLocalStoreDirectory(_:discardingExistingCache:)-1faby"],"anchor":"CloudFileSystemSetup-Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystemSetup"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/cloudfilesystemsetup\/setlocalstoredirectory(_:discardingexistingcache:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"role":"symbol","required":true,"title":"setLocalStoreDirectory(_:discardingExistingCache:)","externalID":"s:9Ensembles20CloudFileSystemSetupP22setLocalStoreDirectory_23discardingExistingCacheySSSg_SbtF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setLocalStoreDirectory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"discardingExistingCache","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setLocalStoreDirectory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"path","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"discardingExistingCache","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event store’s directory, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" when no store is available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"path"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":", any cache already present for this","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"directory must be deleted rather than loaded, and the backend must behave as","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though it had never cached anything. The ensemble passes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"store is being rebuilt, so a device starting over is guaranteed a full fetch","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than a delta against a cursor from a previous incarnation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"discardingExistingCache"}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CustomCloudBackends"]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Backends that cache remote state between launches should store that cache inside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this directory. Doing so ties the cache’s lifetime to the event store’s: when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store is removed or rebuilt, the stale cache goes with it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Caching remote state anywhere with an independent lifetime (the system caches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directory, for instance) is unsafe. Such a cache can outlive the event store it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"describes — surviving even app deletion — and a backend that then resumes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incremental fetch against a rebuilt cloud may never be told about files that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"predate its stale cursor. The device sees a partial cloud and reports no error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Called before priming, whenever the ensemble knows its event store. It is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called for ensemble-independent operations such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/retrieveEnsembleIdentifiers(from:)"},{"text":", so implementations must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tolerate priming without it and simply forgo persistent caching in that case.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tells the file system which local directory belongs to the event store it is serving."}],"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","type":"topic","title":"Ensembles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CloudFileSystemSetup/setLocalStoreDirectory(_:discardingExistingCache:)":{"title":"setLocalStoreDirectory(_:discardingExistingCache:)","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/cloudfilesystemsetup\/setlocalstoredirectory(_:discardingexistingcache:)","abstract":[{"text":"Tells the file system which local directory belongs to the event store it is serving.","type":"text"}],"fragmen